{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_18369",
  "verbalization": "Olaparib, a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor, is implicated in the treatment of several ovarian tumors through its mechanism of action. The evidence suggests that Olaparib may exert therapeutic effects on immature ovarian teratomas through a shared pathway involving cisplatin. This is supported by the observed indications of Olaparib in malignancies such as maligant granulosa cell tumor of the ovary, hereditary site-specific ovarian cancer syndrome, and malignant sex cord stromal tumor of the ovary, all of which are associated with cisplatin. The presence of a common downstream pathway involving cisplatin indicates a potential mechanistic link between Olaparib and immature ovarian teratomas, particularly through the inhibition of cancer cell proliferation or survival. The final scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further validation would be necessary to confirm the direct mechanistic connection.",
